交替来进化自身。\\n<quark-ocr>Load 107 ebdm B0 078 718 C05 a84 643 ba6 b22 b01 aob did8 566 \"a75* 89a a09 18e 0b6 588 154c 991 096 6do 59d G41 fc8 a5 3ab ota</quark-ocr></quark-image>\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">人工生命：动作学习进化论游戏特色</quark-heading>\\n游戏最大的特色在于其AI自主学习机制。开发者中村正义表示，游戏的核心点是让AI自主学习，这在目前技术上是相当难以实现的。游戏弱化了传统生态系统的繁复规则，转而依托引擎自身的动力学反馈，促使这些方块生物发展出不可预判的行为模式与运动形态。游戏具备遗传和自然选择等内在机制，让虚拟生命体具备真实感。开发者希望尖端的机器学习技术最终能让这类游戏中的生物自主进化，从学习如何移动一直到最终“创造出类似文明的东西”。\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">人工生命：动作学习进化论画面表现</quark-heading>\\n游戏采用了抽象简约的艺术风格。在看似简朴的形态之中，这些由基础几何单元构成的虚拟生命体持续呈现出令人意外的生命律动与个体特质。游戏选择了色彩鲜艳的方块生物，而非类人角色，营造出一种温馨而独特的视觉体验。这种设计既降低了视觉复杂度，又让玩家能够更专注于观察生命体在物理规则下的演化过程。\\n游戏图片"}, "10": {"title": "孢子进化论2中文版下载|Evolution of Species 2 安卓版v1.6.53 下载_当游网", "url": "https://www.3h3.com/az/420212.html", "page_content": "游戏类型： 休闲益智 | 游戏大小： 58.38MB\\nEvolution of Species 2 是一款休闲进化模拟手游，玩家在微观世界中扮演造物主，从微小的单细胞生物起步，操控孢子在海洋中狩猎、吞噬，通过不断吸收养分和DNA来强化自身，随着进化等级的提升，解锁多形态的生物特征。\\n<quark-heading level=\"4\">背景设定</quark-heading>\\n1、 微观起源 ：\\n故事始于一个巨大的生命世界，这里充满了未知的生机。玩家化身为最原始的单细胞，置身于广阔的海洋迷宫之中，周围潜伏着各种形态各异的生物。\\n2、 星球生态 ：\\n成千上万的星球构成了宏大的舞台，每个角落都栖息着渴望生存的物种。这里没有绝对的和平，只有永恒的竞争，每一个生命都在为延续基因而努力挣扎。\\n3、 进化之路 ：从简单的细胞结构开始，生命体必须面对严酷的自然选择。通过不断的变异与适应，古老的单细胞将逐步演化成复杂的多细胞生物，开启全新的篇章。\\n4、 生存法则 ：弱肉强食是这片海域唯一的真理。捕食者时刻警惕着猎物，而猎物则拼命寻找安全的藏身之所，每一次遭遇战都可能决定命运的走向。\\n5、 文明萌芽 ：当生命体足够强大，便有机会跨越海洋，探索更广阔的空间。最终目标是建立起属于自己的繁荣群落，在浩瀚宇宙中留下独特的印记。\\n<quark-heading level=\"4\">新手指南</quark-heading>\\n1、可以选择单人游戏和多人游戏\\n2、点击中间三角按钮开始游戏，在旁边可以对孢子进行设置；\\n<quark-ocr>10 T 20013 更多信息</quark-ocr>\\n3、滑动去吃周围的细胞；\\n4、在吃细胞的同时要注意别人的攻击。\\n<quark-heading level=\"4\">玩法机制</quark-heading>\\n1、 吞噬成长 ：\\n滑动屏幕控制方向，主动吞食周围的营养物质或体型较小的生物。每一次成功的吞噬都能增加体积，积累足够的能量以触发下一次关键进化。\\n2、 形态定制 ：利用收集到的基因片段，自由组合身体部位。你可以打造锋利的牙齿用于攻击，也可以装备厚重的甲壳增强防御，完全由自己决定。\\n3、 技能解锁 ：随着等级提升，生物将解锁特殊能力。无论是快速冲刺躲避危险，还是释放毒素麻痹敌人，这些技能在战斗中起到决定性作用。\\n4、 策略对抗 ：面对强大的对手时，单纯依靠体型可能无法取胜。需要观察对方弱点，利用地形优势或特定技能进行周旋，以智取胜才是生存之道。\\n5、 环境适应 ：不同水域拥有不同的温度、酸碱度和压力。玩家需要调整自身属性以适应新环境，否则将难以存活，甚至面临被淘汰的风险。\\n<quark-heading level=\"4\">游戏亮点</quark-heading>\\n1、 丑萌画风 ：\\n采用生动可爱的卡通风格设计生物形象。那些看似怪诞却充满个性的“丑萌”小怪物，给紧张刺激的生存战斗增添了几分趣味与温馨。\\n2、 深度进化 ：\\n提供庞大的进化树供玩家探索。从水生到陆生，从简单到复杂，每一步进化都伴随着外观的巨大变化，带来截然不同的视觉体验。\\n3、 动态器官 ：\\n引入动态器官系统，身体各部分可独立进化。眼睛可以变大获得夜视能力，触手可以变长增加攻击范围，细节之处尽显设计巧思。\\n4、 多样路线 ：\\n不存在单一的通关方式。你可以选择成为独善其身的素食者，也可以做四处猎杀的肉食者，或者成为适应力极强的杂食者，玩法丰富多变。\\n5、 沉浸体验 ：\\n将复杂的生物知识转化为直观有趣的游戏过程。无需枯燥的理论讲解，玩家在操作中自然理解进化原理，享受从零开始的创造乐趣。"}, "11": {"title": "《入侵种》(INVADER) 简要玩法概述 - TapTap 制造脑洞实验室 - TapTap TapTap 制造论坛", "url": "https://www.taptap.cn/moment/781546522100631820", "page_content": "#脑洞实验室 #创作\\n《入侵种》(INVADER) 核心玩法概述\\n这是一款结合了沙盒模拟与生态策略的游戏。你将扮演“造物主”，通过自然语言创造一个入侵物种，将其投放到陌生且残酷的生态系统中，观察它如何生存、繁衍、进化，或是走向灭绝。\\n1. 创造：自然语言造物\\n游戏的核心起点是“创造”。不同于传统的数值调整，你只需要用一段文字描述你的构想，例如：“一种小型、群居、有毒腺的爬行生物，喜欢夜间偷袭”。\\nAI生成：系统会根据你的描述，自动生成物种的外观（模型/纹理）、基础属性（速度/力量/繁殖力）、行为本能（好战/胆小）以及特殊能力（夜视/毒液/拟态）。\\n2. 生态：真实的AI驱动世界\\n当你将物种投放到地图（如丰饶森林、干旱荒漠）中时，真正的挑战才刚刚开始。\\n原住民生态：地图上已存在完整的食物链和原住民生物。\\n独立AI行为：本作中每个生物都有独立的AI决策引擎。它们会根据饥饿、恐惧、领地意识和环境变化实时做出决策。猎食者会评估风险放弃捕食，猎物会利用地形躲藏。\\n动态环境：世界包含季节更替、气候变化和自然灾害，生态平衡极为脆弱，牵一发而动全身。\\n3. 演化：危机中的变异选择\\n这是游戏最独特的机制。当你的物种面临生存压力（如天敌捕食、食物短缺、数量锐减）时，会触发进化时刻。\\n变异选项：AI会根据当前的困境生成3个具体的进化方向。例如，面对飞行天敌，你可以选择“长出硬甲（牺牲速度换防御）”、“发展夜行习性（避开白天）”或“群体防御（增加社会性）”。\\n实时反馈：你的选择将直接改变物种的外观、属性和行为模式，决定种群未来的走向。\\n4. 干预：上帝之手\\n除了观察，你还可以消耗“影响力”直接干预世界进程。\\n手段：从温和的投喂食物、改造地形，到激进的引发洪水、通过基因编辑增强个体，甚至直接抹杀某个天敌物种。\\n策略：你的每一次干预都可能引发蝴蝶效应，需谨慎使用以维持或打破生态平衡。\\n5. 目标：生存与征服\\n游戏不仅仅是无限的沙盒，还包含具有挑战性的战役目标。\\n胜利条件：包括“生态主宰”（站上食物链顶端）、“适应大师”（经历多次变异存活）、“入侵成功”（占领多个区域）等。\\n失败条件：物种彻底灭绝或未在规定时间内达成目标。\\n总结\\n在《入侵种》中，你既是设计者也是观察者。游戏的核心乐趣在于看着自己创造的生命在残酷的自然法则下，通过一次次变异和适应，最终书写出属于它们自己的生存史诗。"}, "12": {"title": "Steam - Evolution of Species 2: Online", "url": "https://store.steampowered.com/app/3290560/Evolution_of_Species_2_Online/?l=tchinese", "page_content": "社群中心\\nEvolution of Species 2: Online\\nEvolution of Species 2: Online\\n開發人員\\nEvolution of Games\\n發行商\\nEvolution of Games\\n發行日\\n2024 年 11 月 1 日\\nWelcome to the world of microscopic creatures! Help your creation evolve from an inconspicuous inhabitant of the microscopic depths into a unique creature that can stand up for itself. Create the most unusual creature! Show it to the world! Fight with other players online!\\n所有評論：\\n3 篇使用者評論 - 使用者評論數量不足，無法產生整體評價\\n發行日期:\\n2024 年 11 月 1 日\\n開發人員:\\nEvolution of Games\\n發行商:\\nEvolution of Games\\n標籤\\n使用者為此產品所選用的熱門標籤：\\n模擬 休閒 生活模擬 自訂角色 生物收集 放鬆 氛圍 可愛 多人 玩家對戰 單人 沙盒 探索 街機 華麗格鬥\\n語言 :\\n11 種支援語言\\n<quark-table><table><tbody><tr><th></th><th>介面</th><th>完整語音</th><th>字幕</th></tr><tr><td>繁體中文</td><td 查看全部 11 種支援的語言\\n內容\\n包含互動元素\\n遊戲內聊天, 線上互動\\n名稱: Evolution of Species 2: Online\\n類型: 冒險 , 休閒 , 獨立製作 , 大型多人連線 , 模擬\\n開發人員: Evolution of Games\\n發行商: Evolution of Games\\n系列作: Evolution of Species\\n發行日期: 2024 年 11 月 1 日\\n造訪網站\\n- Take part in the evolution! Create unique creatures using a flexible customization system, dozens of different body parts and a lot of colors for them. Countless unique combinations!\\n- Choose one of the thousands of planets available for life, fight with its bizarre inhabitants and become the strongest of them!\\n- Develop your creatures in battles with real players around the world. Prove that your creation is invincible!\\n- Share your creations with friends and add their creatures to your game. Find the most unusual life form!\\n- Participate in theme parties and prove that your creature is the best!\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">系統需求</quark-heading>\\n最低配備:\\nDirectX: 版本：9.0\\n儲存空間: 100 MB 可用空間\\n建議配備:\\nDirectX: 版本：9.0\\n儲存空間: 100 MB 可用空間"}, "13": {"title": "Substrate: Emergence 有什么特色内容-游戏特色内容介绍_3DM单机", "url": "https://www.3dmgame.com/gl/3989632.html", "page_content": "《Substrate: Emergence》的竞技场是一只培养皿，玩家要培育会发光的细胞菌落。它们能够突变、聚集成群，也会彼此吞噬，培养皿中的形态因此不断变化。你需要在细致的人工生命模拟中与其他实验室竞争，让自己的菌落繁衍演化，形成独特的生命形态。\\n<quark-ocr>SUBSTRATE EHERGENCE</quark-ocr>\\n在这个模拟细致入微的人工生命沙盒中培育进化：引导你的细胞在生长上压倒对手，尝试各种突变，寻找遗传优势。调控化学反应，并通过直接操控细胞巧妙介入。每个细胞都拥有独特的基因组，决定着它的行为与外观。有的捕猎，有的合作，许多则走向灭绝。宣传图、标志及背景美术由 Daniel Nartov 创作\\n没有两个细胞完全相同。所有机制的灵感均源自真实的细胞生物学，着重呈现涌现的复杂性。细胞拥有由基因决定的功能性细胞器。基因代代相传，不断积累微小的突变，直至进化出新的菌株。资源驱动行为。相互作用会产生你意想不到的涌现效果。简单的有机系统组合在一起，汇聚成一个鲜活的模拟。\\n<quark-ocr>UnDEn A fLUORESCEncE SCOrS</quark-ocr>\\n每一次突变都清晰可见。细胞在消耗资源、复制和竞争时，闪耀着生命的荧光。每一种颜色都映照出它们的遗传密码。\\n每个基因都独立突变，任何细胞都能突变出任意数量的任意基因。\\n<quark-ocr>CONQUER BYOnET</quark-ocr>\\n每个细胞的行为都由一个微型神经网络和遗传算法驱动。没有任何预设脚本。\\n<quark-ocr>BIONET METAMORPH CHARTS 7.0 (4.3-9.7) 7.0 esis(Alpha CILIATE 0213 6°C(24-4 2NODESCAPTURED PLASMODIUM 0121 2TRACKED MANAGE 8mm CONDITIONSVARYACROSSTHIS DISH YOURSTRAINS:CILIATESURVIVES HERE CRYOBANK DEPLOY TO THIS NODE WITH ENTER SPLICER TUTORIAL CILIATE SETTINGS PLASMODIUM CILIATE ? BACK ENTER DRAG MMBDRAG</quark-ocr>\\n<quark-ocr>MASTER SUOLHTYON</quark-ocr>\\n你的细胞并不孤单。培育它们，发展出进化优势，在生长上压倒竞争者。把化学当作武器。夺取区域，控制对手赖以生存的资源。彻底消灭它们。\\n<quark-ocr>DISH OBJECTIVES CAPTURE NEUTRAL DISH EXTRACTTROPHIN TROPHINBANKED16/250mg Grow a varied colony. hoid zo esof the dish withit,then keep your food producers and motile cells. HELD 1/3 TROPHIN 15.91 mg +428.44 μg/s CELLS12 BACTERIA5 MANAGE YLINEAGE NEED MORECELLS NEEDMYORECELLS PINSPECT Hovera cell ororganelle for live stats. Itoggles this panel FILTERSELECTION →M</quark-ocr>\\n为你独特的菌株编目，记录它们的谱系。随着它们蜕变为主宰基质的超级菌株，其价值也会不断攀升。\\n<quark-ocr>LINEAGE LIVE TRY rchstra ® CILIATE CIL-DIG-LYS-A-G9 CIL-DIG-G22 CIL-DIGG82 CIL-DIG-G42 ARCH:CILIATEIDENTIFIED DUO-L-G11 CIL-DIG-G8 GEN0 5DESCENDANTS 5,433 CIL-DIG-G2 CIL-DIG-G6 GENOME·21GENES MEDIAABSORPTION CIL-DIG-G23 CIL-DIG-G5 yield0.01x orption O CIL-DIG-G7 MITOCHONDRION DUO-L-G13 x1mitochondrion DIG-G4 sug0.56x ami1.43x O lip1.01x DUO-L-G9 CIL-DIG- CIL-DI8-G3 CIL-DIG-G O SENESCENCE CIL-DIG-G3 CIL-DIG-G2 CIL-DIG-G72 TROPHOCYTE lifespan 1.00x CIL-DIG-G43 CIL-DIG CHEMISTRIESx5 CIL-DIG-G72 CILIATE LYSOCYTE Explosive#0radius1.5,count-25%, heat+0.15 DUO-L-G10 Catalytic #0 count 2, scale 0.60, DUO-L 4C2-L-G00-L-GUB-L-G11 nic#0 strength 0.3,genes 2, DUO-L-G14 FLAGELLATE bias 0.0 Explc osive→#0radius1.5,count CIL-DIG-G4 CDUO-L-G9 PLASMODIUM Penetrating~#0 threshold0.45,depth CIL-DIG-G62 DUO-L-G10 IG-G22 COLLECTORX2 CIL-DIG-G83 x2collector CIL-L-G11 CIL-DIG-G23 count1 capture 0.990.99x DUO-DIG-G10 CIL-DIG-G43 DIGESTIVEENZYME DUO-L-G142 digestive enzyme CIL-DIG-G62 firerate1.9/s ports3 CIL-DIG-G42 CIL-DIG-G73 reach0.05 CIL-DIG-G9 RENAME ROOT</quark-ocr>\\n开发者的话：我独自开发这款游戏，凭借的是我在细胞神经科学方面的背景，以及作为音乐人和抽象画家的经验。所有游戏系统、模拟架构、视觉设计、程序化美术和音频设计均出自我手。原声音乐由我在几位朋友的帮助下制作。代码库由我一人编写和维护，我以 Claude Code 及其他智能体编程工具作为主要工作流程。所有美术资源均非由生成式 AI 创作，游戏运行时也不会由 AI 生成任何内容。\\n本文内容来源于互联网，如有侵权请联系删除。\\n类型： 模拟经营 发行： Petri Dish Games LLC\\n发售： 2026年9月25日 开发： Petri Dish Games LLC\\n语言： 简中 | 繁中 | 英文 | 日文 | 多国 平台： PC\\n标签： 可爱 物理 探索 人工智能"}, "14": {"title": "Substrate Emergence中文版下载-Substrate Emergence免安装汉化版下载_3DM单机", "url": "https://dl.3dmgame.com/pc/152355.html", "page_content": "<quark-ocr>SUBSTRATE EMERGENCE</quark-ocr>\\n游戏类型： 模拟经营\\n开发厂商： Petri Dish Games LLC\\n更新时间： 2026-10-01\\n发售日期： 2026年9月25日\\n游戏平台： PC\\n游戏语言： 简中\\n标签： 可爱 物理 俯视 探索 人工智能\\n游戏介绍\\n《Substrate: Emergence》 是由Petri Dish Games LLC开发并发行的一款人工生命模拟沙盒游戏，支持简体中文。玩家将在培养皿竞技场中培养荧光细胞菌落，它们会突变、成群结队，还会互相吞噬。在精细的人工生命模拟中与对手实验室一较高下，繁衍出独属于你的生命形态。游戏机制独特，上手难度较高，适合喜欢深度策略的玩家。\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">Substrate: Emergence游戏背景</quark-heading>\\n在这个模拟细致入微的人工生命沙盒中培育进化：引导你的细胞在生长上压倒对手，尝试各种突变，寻找遗传优势。调控化学反应，并通过直接操控细胞巧妙介入。每个细胞都拥有独特的基因组，决定着它的行为与外观。有的捕猎，有的合作，许多则走向灭绝。\\n<quark-ocr>02:151 OBJECTIVES TAKE THE RIVAL'S GERMINAL ZONE ZONESHELD 274 HELD2/4 5.17 μg +0.36 μg/s 67 LINEAGE NSPECT COMPOUNDS INTENSITY 15 RADIUS 1.0 TROPHIN 5.17 TH: a cell aciditied ALKALALKALIN 0.59 or organelle for SULFONACIDIN 1.29 + NO FILTER 123 B0X SELECT COCKEO</quark-ocr>\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">Substrate: Emergence游戏内容</quark-heading>\\n1、没有两个细胞完全相同。所有机制的灵感均源自真实的细胞生物学，着重呈现涌现的复杂性。细胞拥有由基因决定的功能性细胞器。基因代代相传，不断积累微小的突变，直至进化出新的菌株。资源驱动行为。相互作用会产生你意想不到的涌现效果。简单的有机系统组合在一起，汇聚成一个鲜活的模拟。\\n3、每个基因都独立突变，任何细胞都能突变出任意数量的任意基因。\\n4、每个细胞的行为都由一个微型神经网络和遗传算法驱动。没有任何预设脚本。\\n5、你的细胞并不孤单。培育它们，发展出进化优势，在生长上压倒竞争者。把化学当作武器。夺取区域，控制对手赖以生存的资源。彻底消灭它们。\\n6、为你独特的菌株编目，记录它们的谱系。随着它们蜕变为主宰基质的超级菌株，其价值也会不断攀升。\\n<quark-ocr>01:491x OBJECTIVES TAKE THE RIVAL'S GERMINAL ZONE ZONES HELD 1/4 INSPECT SELECTION ↓9 81 22 NTENSITY COMPOUNDS 15 % RADIUS 1.0 u TROPHIN 4 Ciliate x3 8.31 Ciliate k2 ALKALALKALIN 0.59 kedl LOCKED ILTER NO FILTER LOCKED</quark-ocr>\\n游戏图片"}, "15": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution", "url": "https://store.steampowered.com/app/774541/Species_Artificial_Life_Real_Evolution/", "page_content": ""}, "16": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution Gameplay", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_zAFIAgJh1I", "page_content": ""}, "17": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution", "url": "https://steamcommunity.com/app/774541", "page_content": ""}, "18": {"title": "Any evolution simulators better than Species: Artificial Life?", "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/SpeculativeEvolution/comments/r37xw0/any_evolution_simulators_better_than_species/", "page_content": ""}, "19": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution by Jamie Schumacher", "url": "https://www.indiegogo.com/en/projects/jamieschumacher/species-artificial-life-real-evolution", "page_content": "## Project story\n\n## A quick reminder:  \n\n\nThe latest proof-of-concept demo release, v0.4.1 Alpha, is available for you to try out.\n\nPlease remember, this is only a proof-of-concept demo; many, many planned features have not yet been implemented which will be featured in later releases.\n\nDownload Here - (43.5 MB)\n\nInformation on Mouse/Keyboard controls can be found here\n\n\\----------------\n\n## About the goal...  \n\n\nWe're perfectly aware that the campaign isn't going to get anywhere close to our original, over-optimistic goal of 25k. This is primarily because we vastly overestimated our own self-marketing abilities: our pageview stats are... underwhelming, to say the least.\n\nBut this doesn't mean the end of Species. Far from it: we will build this game, at cost if we have to, and since we're using flexible funding the money our contributors have provided will get to us regardless. It will be put towards maintaining the website and paying our artist.\n\nBut I just want to make something very very clear:\n\nSpecies will still get made.\n\nOne way or another, we're going to make this game a reality.\n\nAny last-minute contributions would still of course still be a huge help in making sure we stay out of the black for as long as possible, so please don't let the original goal keep you from contributing. \n\n\\----------------\n\n### What is Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution?\n\n### Species is a game about macroscopic-scale evolution using a scientifically accurate simulation that you can explore and interact with, and even perform some science of your own.  \n\n\n### To be more precise, Species is a scientifically-accurate natural-selection simulator which allows you to experience evolution first-hand, simulated from the very first principles of evolutionary science:\n\n  * Variation (every creature is uniquely defined by it’s genes),\n  * Mutation (child creatures are randomly modified versions of their parents), and \n  * Natural Selection (the environment affects every creature in their struggle to survive).\n\n\n\nWith these principles as it’s gameplay mechanics, Species recreates the same unguided pressures that drove the development of all life on earth over the last 4 billion years.\n\n### Whether you just want to observe, watching and studying as the tree of life constructs itself from a single species, or you want to be an active influence on the development of the species in the game, is up to you.\n\nA group of creatures in the game, each randomly generated.  \nYes, the green one terrifies us too.\n\nThere are many good academic evolution simulators across the Internet, evolving colours, numbers, text or even single celled organisms. There are also many games, claiming to be based on the science of evolution, but which actually implement none of the mechanics behind evolution.\n\nSpecies is something new: both a game, accessible and entertaining, allowing you to explore a large 3D world filled with hundreds of unique, procedurally-generated creatures... and a evolutionary simulator, implemented from the ground up with the intention of making a realistic and genuine model of evolution.\n\nWith herbivores and carnivores, combat, mating, behavioral and physiological evolution, population dynamics like extinctions and explosions, speciation, and many more features to come, the world of Species is a complex, rich, and adaptive environment, featuring:\n\nA detailed, macroscopic 3D world: the first of it's kind in a natural selection simulator, filled with hundreds of unique procedurally-generated creatures all competing for survival.\n\nGenuine natural selection: No fitness function, no predefined goals: just survival. The player can aid and interact with the simulation, but they will never control it.\n\nA scientific approach: Evolution, speciation, extinction: these are not a direct functions of the game, they're natural effects of the game's mechanics.\n\nProcedural gameplay: whether you start from a group of slug-worms or generate a population of random creatures, the game carves out it’s own history full of population explosions, speciations and the extinctions of the uncompetitive or just plain unlucky.\n\nReal-time evolution: Select a species, accelerate time, and watch as it’s shape and stats morph in front of your eyes.\n\nThat's one suspicious-looking cactus.\n\nWhen we first learned that this hadn’t been done before, our reaction was surprise. Out of all the time and energy invested in video games and scientific simulations both, how was it possible that a proper evolution game didn’t already exist? After all, we wanted to play it, so surely others did too?\n\nBut we came to realise: this was something that genuinely hadn’t been done before. A variety of vaguely similar things had been done, but nothing quite like this. So we set out to do it.\n\nSometimes, that’s all the reason you need.\n\n### So, why Indiegogo?\n\nSpecies has been in the works, in some form or another, for the past 8 years or so. In that time, it's developed a long way, and recently has begun growing in leaps and bounds. A year ago, the first public dev videos were released, and the feedback and support we recieved from everyone was very encouraging, and we're ready to take the next step forward in development.\n\nWe've been working hard to bring the game up to a high standard both in the simulation and design aspects alike, but now it has reached the point where our work on Species has hit the harsh reality of the real world, and the commitments real life brings with it.\n\nWe chose to go with Indiegogo becuase it is a more accessible funding platform to those outside the US, as we in the Species development team are, in the hope that we would be able to raise enough funding to support ourselves during the game's development.\n\nTo that end, funding from Indiegogo will be used for:\n\nKeeping the developers alive: Enough funding to keep our development team fed, sheltered, and clothed for a year while they work full-time on Species.\n\n  \nWeb hosting: Funding to keep the site, forums, and download services online, as well as the ability to provide online multiplayer in later releases.\n\nSpeaking of Online Multiplayer: Keeping our goals reasonable, there won't be any kind of attempt at making Species into an MMO. But something that can plausibly be added is the ability to physically connect players' maps together, combining their CPU power and creating a potentially limitless online overworld. This is possibly the single most ambitious and difficult-to-implement feature on the list, but if we can do it, it would mean the difference between a self-contained petrie-dish world, and a planet.\n\nSound and Music: Species is going to need a lot of help with audio, which is currently being provided by Brain Sugar. Funding from Indiegogo will keep him on the team, in order to provide a full soundtrack for the game throughout its development.\n\nConcept, Art, and Design: In order to become a fully fleshed out world, Species not only needs audio, but striking visuals as well, currently being provided by our graphic designer, Jade Taggart. On top of both environment and creature work, Jade is also developing the UI and (planned) vehicle and structure concepts for Species; funding from Indiegogo will help keep her on the team to continue her work.\n\nAnd most importantly, Expanding the game: We're dedicated to seeing Species achieve as much of it's potential as it possibly can, and Indiegogo funding can go a long way towards achieving that goal.\n\nWith your help, here are a selection of the features we hope to implement in the future:\n\n  * A fully realised ecosystem, where every system impacts and influences every other system, resulting in emergent and unpredictable natural selection pressures.  \nAmong the features already planned are flight, water bodies for aquatic and amphibious animals, variable temperature and humidity, growing and migrating forests (made out of reproducing trees with hereditary characteristics, no less), basic forms of symbiosis and parasitic behavior, and others.\n\n\n  * Every conceivable biological niche open for the creatures in the game to fill.  \nWe want to give them the freedom to evolve into anything, from realistic to fanciful, blind cave-dwelling dinosaurs to giant carnivorous insects, hydrogen-filled organic blimps to schools of sea-dwelling plankton-filtering birds.\n\n\n\n  * Engaging, science-inspired Gameplay: Although the game will always remain a relatively open sandbox and won't have any predefined win-conditions, you'll be able to apply artificial selection pressures.By running them over with a robotic chainsaw rover.  \nOn top of that horrifyingly awesome thought, you can change the creatures with direct genetic manipulation, change the climate and ecosystem for the better or worse, dynamically build the in-game Tree Of Life by collecting samples and finding fossils, trigger disasters, and do awesome SCIENCE™.\n  * Complete Modability: A healthy community is key to a successful independant game. By opening as many segments of the game as possible to modding, we can help grow the community. And by using and making online mods, you the community will be able to help unlock far more of Species potential than we developers could do on our own!\n\n\n\n  * Mac/Linux Implementation: Species is built with Microsoft XNA Game Studio software, which means it’s not natively supported outside of Windows... but we intend to put some research into the matter, to learn what we can. Although we can't promise anything on this particular front, we do hope to make the game as platform-independant as we possibly can.\n\n\n\n### Who are you people?  \n  \n\n\n  * James Schumacher (Quasar), an Independant Games Programmer and the Lead Developer on Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution.   \nI've been programming indie games since I was 16 and have 5 years professional experience, plus 7 years of slightly-less-professional experience debating creationists on the internet. The two interests combined together in the project that became Species ALRE, which I have been working on on an on/off basis since 2007, and consistantly since 2011.\n  * Jade Taggart (CrashKat), the artsy person! Freelance digital artist and graphic designer for Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution.\n\n\n\nI specialize in game art and design, which I've been doing for nearly 10 years and hold two degrees in, as well as experience in web development and specialist consulting. While my dev skill lies mostly in 3D content creation and delivery, I also do animation, special effects and 2D artwork.\n\nProfessionally, I currently work for CyberKat Hosting as Senior Graphics Designer, and I also provide digital content and specialist consulting on a freelance basis.\n\n##   \n  \n\\-----------   \n\n\n## MOUSE/KEYBOARD CONTROLS  \nFor use with Alpha 0.4.1 Demo release.  \n\n\nCamera\n\n  * Hold Right Click to rotate the camera.\n  * Use W,A,S,D to move, hold shift to \"sprint\"\n  * Press Spacebar to toggle camera fall on/off.\n  * Press C to lock the camera around the current creature.\n\n\n\n  \nOther Controls\n\n  * Click to select a Creature, or a Species if in that mode.\n  * Click their respective icons on the left (next to the statistics) to change between Creature, Species and Ecosystem modes.\n  * Click the Details button to learn more about the current creature, species or world depending on mode.\n  * Click the Time Accelleration buttons (or press ~, 1, 2 or 3) to change the simulation speed.\n  * Click the Highlight Filter to get a visual display of various statistics across all creatures on the map.\n  * Click the tool icons to activate different interaction tools: \n    * Click a creature to feed\n    * Click a creature to kill\n    * Click a creature to take a gene sample, then click another to splice it into that creatures genome. The spliced creature will then give birth to gene-spliced creatures.\n    * Click and hold over a creature to irradiate it. The irradiated creature will then give birth to heavily mutated offspring.\n\n\n\n## Rewards\n\n## Looking for the best value?\n\nUse our product comparison tool to choose the best pledge for you and make sure you've added everything you wanted."}, "20": {"title": "Artificial Life, Real Evolution Gameplay (Species Game)", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ELdRw14jNFg", "page_content": ""}, "21": {"title": "Species Evolution Simulator - Apps on Google Play", "url": "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.GardenofDreams.SpeciesEvolution", "page_content": ""}, "22": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution | Vinesauce Wiki - Fandom", "url": "https://vinesauce.fandom.com/wiki/Species:_Artificial_Life,_Real_Evolution", "page_content": ""}, "23": {"title": "Species Artificial Life Real Evolution Download - Explore the ...", "url": "https://species-artificial-life-real-evolution.software.informer.com/", "page_content": ""}, "24": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life Real Evolution", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8eb_rkUgYEU", "page_content": ""}, "25": {"title": "My Review of the Game :: Species: Artificial Life, Real ...", "url": "https://steamcommunity.com/app/774541/discussions/0/3075370124707956701/", "page_content": "安装 Steam \n\n登录 | 语言 \n\n繁體中文（繁体中文） 日本語（日语） 한국어（韩语） ไทย（泰语） български（保加利亚语） Čeština（捷克语） Dansk（丹麦语） Deutsch（德语） English（英语） Español-España（西班牙语 - 西班牙） Español - Latinoamérica（西班牙语 - 拉丁美洲） Ελληνικά（希腊语） Français（法语） Italiano（意大利语） Bahasa Indonesia（印度尼西亚语） Magyar（匈牙利语） Nederlands（荷兰语） Norsk（挪威语） Polski（波兰语） Português（葡萄牙语 - 葡萄牙） Português-Brasil（葡萄牙语 - 巴西） Română（罗马尼亚语） Русский（俄语） Suomi（芬兰语） Svenska（瑞典语） Türkçe（土耳其语） Tiếng Việt（越南语） Українська（乌克兰语） 报告翻译问题"}, "26": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution Reviews", "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/game/species-artificial-life-real-evolution/", "page_content": "X \n\nMetascore Critic reviews are not available yet \n\ntbd\n\nUser Score User reviews are not available yet \n\ntbd\n\ntbd\n\ntbd\n\ntbd\n\nSummary Play with evolution! Species: ALRE is a scientifically-grounded, emergent simulation of natural selection. Creatures evolve and speciate in response to in-game mutation and selection forces, allowing you to experience and tinker with evolution in real-time.\n\nPlatforms: \n\n  * PC\n\n\n\nGenres:"}, "27": {"title": "Artificial Life, Real Evolution - Experimental Build Game Review", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_CkNoLp-wxg", "page_content": ""}, "28": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution - Screenwise", "url": "https://screenwiseapp.com/media/species-artificial-life-real-evolution-game", "page_content": "## The \"Spore\" antidote\n\nIf your kid played Spore and felt cheated by the fact that adding a third eye didn't actually change how the creature functioned, Species: ALRE is the remedy. Most \"evolution\" games are just dress-up simulators where you pick a cool-looking wing and get a +5 to flying. This game is different because it’s unfeeling.\n\nThe simulation doesn't care if your creature is cute. It only cares if the creature can reach its food and survive long enough to pass on its messy, mutated DNA. It’s the digital equivalent of a high-end ant farm where you can also trigger a localized ice age just to see who survives. If they've already exhausted the more approachable titles in the ultimate guide to fun and educational biology games, this is the logical \"level up\" into serious simulation.\n\n## Dealing with the jank\n\nWe have to talk about the stability issues. This is a passion project from a tiny developer, and it plays like one. It’s unstable. You will see reviews on Steam and Reddit complaining about crashes, and they aren't exaggerating.\n\nFor a certain type of kid—the one who builds complex redstone machines in Minecraft or spends hours in Kerbal Space Program—the technical friction is just part of the tax you pay for a deep simulation. For everyone else, it’s a deal-breaker. If your kid loses thirty minutes of evolutionary progress because the game closed to desktop, they’re going to be livid. Tell them to save often—basically every time a significant mutation sticks.\n\n## Real science, real slow\n\nThe gameplay loop is meditative, which is a polite way of saying it’s slow. You aren't \"playing\" so much as you are \"tinkering and observing.\" You might spend an hour tweaking the temperature and vegetation levels just to see if a specific limb mutation becomes dominant.\n\nIt’s an incredible tool for understanding things like genetic drift and speciation, but it requires a high level of autonomy. There are no quest markers or NPCs telling you what to do. If your kid needs a narrative hook to stay engaged, they’ll find this boring within twenty minutes. But if they’re the type who watches \"What Da Math\" or other science-heavy YouTube channels, they’ll appreciate that the game treats them like a researcher rather than a toddler.\n\n## The \"Climate\" alternative\n\nIf the technical bugs are too much of a hurdle but the concept of natural selection is still a hit, look into the board game Evolution: Climate. It covers similar ground—adapting to environments and food scarcity—without the risk of a software crash. However, for the kid who wants to see the actual geometry of a creature change over a thousand generations, there is nothing else quite like Species. It’s a flawed, brilliant, frustrating mess of a lab experiment."}, "29": {"title": "Darwinning: Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution", "url": "https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/darwinning-species-artificial-life-real-evolution", "page_content": "# Darwinning: Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution\n\n  \nI think if this footage of Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution shows anything, it's that gamers should not be allowed anywhere near a first-contact situation. What happens in this sandbox natural selection sim, where you watch species evolve rapidly as they deal with the changes in the climate and food chain, is just a little bit genocidey. Everything is going fine: the creatures crawl from the ooze that they once called home, they scamper over the world, they get a bit too numerous so an ice-age is set in motion for a little bit of population control, then the developer sets a deathbot loose. The selection gets a little bit unnatural at that point.  \n  \nThe Galapagos as a design document is a fun idea. There are a huge amount of variables to play with: the climate, the water level, the fertility. Then there's more unnatural enhancements, with you directly affecting the creatures mating habits, or physically plucking one from the ground to place elsewhere on the little island. Any physical stat you can think of can be exposed in the game engine: want to know a particular creature's neck width? There's a toggle for that. And global extinction is just a few toggles away. In this instance, the rover the developer sets loose kills all the low-strength creatures and feeds the high-strenth ones, but then they get reliant on the rover's lunch runs. So when he takes the rover away, the entire civilisation collapses. \n\nThere's not a lot of game yet, but that's coming. The simulation is what matters first and foremost, but when that's settled there will be species vs species fights to the death, terraforming, and fossil hunting.\n\nSpecies: Artificial Life, Real Evolution 0.6.0 Gameplay Trailer \n\nThe alpha builds will be free forever, but you can buy-in to the latest versions."}, "30": {"title": "Artificial Life, Real Evolution Free Download (v0.14.2.7)", "url": "https://gogunlocked.com/species-artificial-life-real-evolution-free-download/", "page_content": ""}, "31": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution - I'm back", "url": "https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/774541/view/5832739282294831223", "page_content": "Install Steam \n\nsign in | language \n\n简体中文 (Simplified Chinese) 繁體中文 (Traditional Chinese) 日本語 (Japanese) 한국어 (Korean) ไทย (Thai) Bahasa Indonesia (Indonesian) Bahasa Melayu (Malay) BETA Български (Bulgarian) Čeština (Czech) Dansk (Danish) Deutsch (German) Español - España (Spanish - Spain) Español - Latinoamérica (Spanish - Latin America) Ελληνικά (Greek) Français (French) Italiano (Italian) Magyar (Hungarian) Nederlands (Dutch) Norsk (Norwegian) Polski (Polish) Português (Portuguese - Portugal) Português - Brasil (Portuguese - Brazil) Română (Romanian) Русский (Russian) Suomi (Finnish) Svenska (Swedish) Türkçe (Turkish) Tiếng Việt (Vietnamese) Українська (Ukrainian) Report a translation problem"}, "32": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution", "url": "https://steamcommunity.com/app/774541/allnews/", "page_content": ""}, "33": {"title": "Species: Artificial Life, Real Evolution Patches and Updates", "url"